<header>
        <h1>Limit Order Entry Techniques For Long Term Traders</h1>
        <p>"you don't necessarily need the big turning points at the top or the bottoms you just need to meet in between and be a long-term trader still"</p>
    </header>

    <nav>
        <a href="#definition">Definition</a>
        <a href="#prerequisites">Prerequisites</a>
        <a href="#buy-limit">Buy Limit</a>
        <a href="#sell-limit">Sell Limit</a>
        <a href="#alignment">PD Array Alignment</a>
        <a href="#psychology">Market Psychology</a>
        <a href="#example">Example Analysis</a>
        <a href="#study">Study</a>
    </nav>

    <main>
        <section id="definition">
            <h2>Definition</h2>
            <blockquote class="quote">
                <p><em>"using limit entry techniques for long-term traders"</em></p>
            </blockquote>
            <blockquote class="quote">
                <p><em>"you don't necessarily need the big turning points at the top or the bottoms you just need to meet in between and be a long-term trader still and it capitalizes on a lot of pips a lot of points if you do these types of trades"</em></p>
            </blockquote>
            <blockquote class="quote">
                <p><em>"it takes a long time for them to come to fruition and long time for them to set up"</em></p>
            </blockquote>
        </section>

        <section id="prerequisites">
            <h2>Prerequisites & Context</h2>
            <h3>Higher Time Frame Alignment</h3>
            <blockquote class="quote">
                <p><em>"you have to blend the pd arrays on the daily chart as well so by blending these things together with the higher time frame monthly and weekly pulling price one side or the other bullish or bearish respective on those higher time frame charts"</em></p>
            </blockquote>

            <h3>Market Structure Requirement</h3>
            <blockquote class="quote">
                <p><em>"preferably this is going to be useful to you when the market's already shown the willingness to have a market structure break it's already started to move higher"</em></p>
            </blockquote>
        </section>

        <section id="buy-limit">
            <h2>Buying With A Limit Order</h2>

            <h3>Setup Conditions</h3>
            <div class="concept-card">
                <div class="card-header">
                    <span class="card-title">Monthly/Weekly Requirement</span>
                </div>
                <p><em>"the monthly and or weekly should suggest institutional order flow will be seeking a pd array above daily market price"</em></p>
            </div>

            <div class="concept-card">
                <div class="card-header">
                    <span class="card-title">Daily Chart Requirement</span>
                </div>
                <p><em>"the daily should post a bearish candle"</em></p>
                <p><em>"the daily chart must close the candle with a down close and it is not valid while the daily chart candle is trading and or forming"</em></p>
            </div>

            <h3>Entry Placement</h3>
            <blockquote class="quote">
                <p><em>"the buy limit is going to be placed at the bearish candles close this is a daily candle"</em></p>
            </blockquote>

            <svg viewBox="0 0 800 400" xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg">
                <!-- Title -->
                <text x="400" y="30" fill="#ffa502" font-size="20" font-weight="bold" text-anchor="middle">Buy Limit Entry - Down Close Daily Candle</text>

                <!-- Price axis -->
                <line x1="50" y1="80" x2="50" y2="350" stroke="#9898a8" stroke-width="2"/>
                <text x="30" y="85" fill="#e8e8ed" font-size="12" text-anchor="middle">Price</text>

                <!-- Time axis -->
                <line x1="50" y1="350" x2="750" y2="350" stroke="#9898a8" stroke-width="2"/>
                <text x="400" y="380" fill="#e8e8ed" font-size="12" text-anchor="middle">Time (Daily Candles)</text>

                <!-- Bearish candle (down close) -->
                <rect x="200" y="150" width="80" height="120" fill="#ff4757" stroke="#ff4757" stroke-width="2"/>
                <line x1="240" y1="120" x2="240" y2="150" stroke="#ff4757" stroke-width="3"/>
                <line x1="240" y1="270" x2="240" y2="300" stroke="#ff4757" stroke-width="3"/>

                <!-- Labels for candle parts -->
                <text x="300" y="130" fill="#e8e8ed" font-size="14">Daily High</text>
                <line x1="240" y1="120" x2="290" y2="125" stroke="#9898a8" stroke-width="1" stroke-dasharray="2,2"/>

                <text x="300" y="165" fill="#e8e8ed" font-size="14">Daily Open</text>
                <line x1="280" y1="150" x2="290" y2="160" stroke="#9898a8" stroke-width="1" stroke-dasharray="2,2"/>

                <text x="300" y="280" fill="#ffa502" font-size="14" font-weight="bold">Daily Close (Down Close)</text>
                <line x1="280" y1="270" x2="290" y2="275" stroke="#ffa502" stroke-width="2"/>

                <text x="300" y="310" fill="#e8e8ed" font-size="14">Daily Low</text>
                <line x1="240" y1="300" x2="290" y2="305" stroke="#9898a8" stroke-width="1" stroke-dasharray="2,2"/>

                <!-- Buy limit line -->
                <line x1="100" y1="270" x2="700" y2="270" stroke="#2ed573" stroke-width="3" stroke-dasharray="8,4"/>
                <text x="550" y="265" fill="#2ed573" font-size="16" font-weight="bold">BUY LIMIT at Close</text>

                <!-- Next candle (goes below close) -->
                <rect x="400" y="260" width="80" height="60" fill="#2ed573" stroke="#2ed573" stroke-width="2"/>
                <line x1="440" y1="250" x2="440" y2="260" stroke="#2ed573" stroke-width="3"/>
                <line x1="440" y1="320" x2="440" y2="340" stroke="#2ed573" stroke-width="3"/>

                <!-- Arrow showing fill below close -->
                <path d="M 440 290 L 440 330" stroke="#ffa502" stroke-width="3" fill="none" marker-end="url(#arrowhead)"/>
                <text x="460" y="315" fill="#ffa502" font-size="14" font-weight="bold">Filled here</text>

                <!-- Arrow marker -->
                <defs>
                    <marker id="arrowhead" markerWidth="10" markerHeight="10" refX="5" refY="5" orient="auto">
                        <polygon points="0 0, 10 5, 0 10" fill="#ffa502"/>
                    </marker>
                </defs>

                <!-- Annotation -->
                <text x="400" y="370" fill="#9898a8" font-size="13" text-anchor="middle">"the very next day or the next candle when it opens up we're expecting</text>
                <text x="400" y="390" fill="#9898a8" font-size="13" text-anchor="middle">price movement to move below that down candles close"</text>
            </svg>

            <h3>What This Accomplishes</h3>
            <blockquote class="quote">
                <p><em>"the very next day or the next candle when it opens up we're expecting price movement to move below that down candles close"</em></p>
            </blockquote>
            <blockquote class="quote">
                <p><em>"what we're actually doing is we're buying at a deeply undervalued price it's already going to be oversold without requiring any indicators but we're going to be buying at a deep deep discount when the market's predisposed to move higher"</em></p>
            </blockquote>
            <blockquote class="quote">
                <p><em>"you're buying that real deep suppressed undervalued market and it's in a deep discount and it will look to seek to move to a premium"</em></p>
            </blockquote>
        </section>

        <section id="sell-limit">
            <h2>Selling With Limit Orders</h2>

            <h3>Setup Conditions</h3>
            <div class="concept-card">
                <div class="card-header">
                    <span class="card-title">Monthly/Weekly Requirement</span>
                </div>
                <p><em>"the monthly and or weekly should suggest institutional order flow will be seeking pd arrays below daily market price"</em></p>
            </div>

            <div class="concept-card">
                <div class="card-header">
                    <span class="card-title">Daily Chart Requirement</span>
                </div>
                <p><em>"the daily should post a bullish candle and the daily chart must close the candle with a up close"</em></p>
                <p><em>"it is not valid while the daily chart candle is trading and or forming"</em></p>
            </div>

            <h3>Entry Placement</h3>
            <blockquote class="quote">
                <p><em>"the sell limit is going to be placed at the bullish candles close"</em></p>
            </blockquote>

            <svg viewBox="0 0 800 400" xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg">
                <!-- Title -->
                <text x="400" y="30" fill="#ffa502" font-size="20" font-weight="bold" text-anchor="middle">Sell Limit Entry - Up Close Daily Candle</text>

                <!-- Price axis -->
                <line x1="50" y1="80" x2="50" y2="350" stroke="#9898a8" stroke-width="2"/>
                <text x="30" y="85" fill="#e8e8ed" font-size="12" text-anchor="middle">Price</text>

                <!-- Time axis -->
                <line x1="50" y1="350" x2="750" y2="350" stroke="#9898a8" stroke-width="2"/>
                <text x="400" y="380" fill="#e8e8ed" font-size="12" text-anchor="middle">Time (Daily Candles)</text>

                <!-- Bullish candle (up close) -->
                <rect x="200" y="180" width="80" height="120" fill="#2ed573" stroke="#2ed573" stroke-width="2"/>
                <line x1="240" y1="150" x2="240" y2="180" stroke="#2ed573" stroke-width="3"/>
                <line x1="240" y1="300" x2="240" y2="330" stroke="#2ed573" stroke-width="3"/>

                <!-- Labels for candle parts -->
                <text x="300" y="160" fill="#e8e8ed" font-size="14">Daily High</text>
                <line x1="240" y1="150" x2="290" y2="155" stroke="#9898a8" stroke-width="1" stroke-dasharray="2,2"/>

                <text x="300" y="195" fill="#ffa502" font-size="14" font-weight="bold">Daily Close (Up Close)</text>
                <line x1="280" y1="180" x2="290" y2="190" stroke="#ffa502" stroke-width="2"/>

                <text x="300" y="310" fill="#e8e8ed" font-size="14">Daily Open</text>
                <line x1="280" y1="300" x2="290" y2="305" stroke="#9898a8" stroke-width="1" stroke-dasharray="2,2"/>

                <text x="300" y="340" fill="#e8e8ed" font-size="14">Daily Low</text>
                <line x1="240" y1="330" x2="290" y2="335" stroke="#9898a8" stroke-width="1" stroke-dasharray="2,2"/>

                <!-- Sell limit line -->
                <line x1="100" y1="180" x2="700" y2="180" stroke="#ff4757" stroke-width="3" stroke-dasharray="8,4"/>
                <text x="550" y="175" fill="#ff4757" font-size="16" font-weight="bold">SELL LIMIT at Close</text>

                <!-- Next candle (goes above close) -->
                <rect x="400" y="140" width="80" height="60" fill="#ff4757" stroke="#ff4757" stroke-width="2"/>
                <line x1="440" y1="120" x2="440" y2="140" stroke="#ff4757" stroke-width="3"/>
                <line x1="440" y1="200" x2="440" y2="220" stroke="#ff4757" stroke-width="3"/>

                <!-- Arrow showing fill above close -->
                <path d="M 440 170 L 440 130" stroke="#ffa502" stroke-width="3" fill="none" marker-end="url(#arrowhead2)"/>
                <text x="460" y="155" fill="#ffa502" font-size="14" font-weight="bold">Filled here</text>

                <!-- Arrow marker -->
                <defs>
                    <marker id="arrowhead2" markerWidth="10" markerHeight="10" refX="5" refY="5" orient="auto">
                        <polygon points="0 0, 10 5, 0 10" fill="#ffa502"/>
                    </marker>
                </defs>

                <!-- Annotation -->
                <text x="400" y="370" fill="#9898a8" font-size="13" text-anchor="middle">"it has to be above this particular candles close"</text>
            </svg>

            <h3>What This Accomplishes</h3>
            <blockquote class="quote">
                <p><em>"what we're doing is essentially we're selling short in an overvalued or overbought condition in a market that's predisposed to go lower based on monthly and or weekly pd arrays that will draw price lower"</em></p>
            </blockquote>
            <blockquote class="quote">
                <p><em>"by selling short on a limit above that candles close what you're doing is essentially getting that last little piece of market movement above getting that last little surge"</em></p>
            </blockquote>
        </section>

        <section id="alignment">
            <h2>PD Array Alignment Requirement</h2>

            <blockquote class="quote">
                <p><em>"you're not just selling on a limit on any up candle if we have an opinion about being bearish"</em></p>
            </blockquote>

            <blockquote class="quote">
                <p><em>"these conditions are best suited when we align them with a daily pd array in other words if there's a bearish order block if there's a gap that it's traded into if it's filled in a void if it's traded above a recent high okay or it's retreat back into an old historical low support broken analysis resistance"</em></p>
            </blockquote>

            <blockquote class="quote">
                <p><em>"you're not just indiscriminately going out and finding up candles and down candles... you're not just simply going in based on the candle itself by itself it's not a be all end-all and a system in and of itself"</em></p>
            </blockquote>

            <div class="concept-card">
                <div class="card-header">
                    <span class="card-title">Critical Alignment Rule</span>
                </div>
                <p><em>"you have to blend the pd arrays on the daily chart as well so by blending these things together with the higher time frame monthly and weekly pulling price one side or the other bullish or bearish respective on those higher time frame charts"</em></p>
            </div>

            <h3>For Bearish Setups</h3>
            <blockquote class="quote">
                <p><em>"on monthly and weekly if you're expecting lower prices or bearish pd arrays that should draw price down to a discount what you're expecting to see on the daily is up movement to go to a short term premium when that occurs then you have really really low risk high probability entry patterns at your disposal"</em></p>
            </blockquote>
        </section>

        <section id="psychology">
            <h2>Market Psychology & Logic</h2>

            <h3>Why Buy Limits Work (Bullish)</h3>
            <blockquote class="quote">
                <p><em>"what we're actually doing is we're buying at a deeply undervalued price it's already going to be oversold without requiring any indicators but we're going to be buying at a deep deep discount when the market's predisposed to move higher"</em></p>
            </blockquote>

            <blockquote class="quote">
                <p><em>"you get quick immediate feedback even on a daily basis that you're on the right side of the marketplace and you start seeing profitability almost immediately"</em></p>
            </blockquote>

            <h3>Why Sell Limits Work (Bearish)</h3>
            <blockquote class="quote">
                <p><em>"we're getting this up movement against what longer term institutional order flows suggesting again on monthly and or weekly chart"</em></p>
            </blockquote>

            <blockquote class="quote">
                <p><em>"many times when we look at day trades you're going to see that that's many times what you'll see is the judah swing it'll open make the high in london and then sell off and it'll be the beginning of a long long term move in that particular pair or asset"</em></p>
            </blockquote>

            <h3>Premium vs Discount Context</h3>
            <blockquote class="quote">
                <p><em>"the market's undervalued in already primarily bullish market condition"</em></p>
            </blockquote>
            <blockquote class="quote">
                <p><em>"it's in a deep discount and it will look to seek to move to a premium"</em></p>
            </blockquote>
        </section>

        <section id="example">
            <h2>Japanese Yen Example Analysis</h2>

            <h3>Weekly Context</h3>
            <blockquote class="quote">
                <p><em>"you can see how price was moving away from that 100 level and there was a bearish order block up around that 118 119 level and that was the weekly premium pd array that would draw price up to that level long long term"</em></p>
            </blockquote>

            <blockquote class="quote">
                <p><em>"we saw a bullish order block down in the discount level at 100 so you saw the willingness to want to bounce off that level"</em></p>
            </blockquote>

            <h3>Specific Entry Points & Results</h3>
            <div class="concept-card">
                <div class="card-header">
                    <span class="card-title">September Entry</span>
                </div>
                <p><em>"we saw a september rally away from a previous order block that was formed in august 2016 september we saw it retrade back down into it and using the down candle the very next day it did trade down below the close giving an amazing fill"</em></p>
                <p><strong>Result:</strong> <em>"from that point all the way up to the weekly pd array or bearish order block it's 1800 pips"</em></p>
            </div>

            <div class="concept-card">
                <div class="card-header">
                    <span class="card-title">November Entry</span>
                </div>
                <p><em>"in november during the post election rally of donald trump's election in the u.s price stabbed one more time down into that weekly bullish order block"</em></p>
                <p><strong>Result:</strong> <em>"from that point up to the weekly weekly pd array up at the weekly bearish order block was 980 pips"</em></p>
            </div>

            <div class="concept-card">
                <div class="card-header">
                    <span class="card-title">Additional Entries</span>
                </div>
                <p><em>"the next down close on this daily chart here again using the close of that down candle as a buy limit order entry point that next candle puts you in a position where it would have been 785 pip move"</em></p>
                <p><em>"the next down candle again comes in with a 600 pip rally"</em></p>
                <p><em>"another one comes in at 500 pips"</em></p>
                <p><em>"the last one right before it gets to the weekly pd array given a 360 pip price move"</em></p>
            </div>

            <h3>Key Observations</h3>
            <blockquote class="quote">
                <p><em>"each down candles close the next day it trades down below it you would be filled only limit going long and look at the responsiveness of price immediately after that there's one two three four five examples here on this daily time frame"</em></p>
            </blockquote>

            <blockquote class="quote">
                <p><em>"that move from the 980 pip move it's essentially the equilibrium price bar just below it and even above the equilibrium price point there was many opportunities where you could have got several hundred pips"</em></p>
            </blockquote>
        </section>

        <section id="study">
            <h2>Study & Review</h2>
            <p>Click each card to reveal the answer (from transcript quotes)</p>

            <div class="flashcard-container">
                <div class="flashcard" onclick="this.classList.toggle('revealed')">
                    <div class="flashcard-question">What are the monthly/weekly requirements for a buy limit entry?</div>
                    <div class="flashcard-answer">"the monthly and or weekly should suggest institutional order flow will be seeking a pd array above daily market price"</div>
                </div>

                <div class="flashcard" onclick="this.classList.toggle('revealed')">
                    <div class="flashcard-question">What must the daily chart show for a buy limit entry?</div>
                    <div class="flashcard-answer">"the daily should post a bearish candle" and "the daily chart must close the candle with a down close and it is not valid while the daily chart candle is trading and or forming"</div>
                </div>

                <div class="flashcard" onclick="this.classList.toggle('revealed')">
                    <div class="flashcard-question">Where exactly is the buy limit placed?</div>
                    <div class="flashcard-answer">"the buy limit is going to be placed at the bearish candles close"</div>
                </div>

                <div class="flashcard" onclick="this.classList.toggle('revealed')">
                    <div class="flashcard-question">What happens the next day after placing a buy limit at a down close?</div>
                    <div class="flashcard-answer">"the very next day or the next candle when it opens up we're expecting price movement to move below that down candles close"</div>
                </div>

                <div class="flashcard" onclick="this.classList.toggle('revealed')">
                    <div class="flashcard-question">What are you accomplishing by buying below the down candle's close?</div>
                    <div class="flashcard-answer">"what we're actually doing is we're buying at a deeply undervalued price it's already going to be oversold without requiring any indicators but we're going to be buying at a deep deep discount when the market's predisposed to move higher"</div>
                </div>

                <div class="flashcard" onclick="this.classList.toggle('revealed')">
                    <div class="flashcard-question">Where is the sell limit placed for bearish setups?</div>
                    <div class="flashcard-answer">"the sell limit is going to be placed at the bullish candles close"</div>
                </div>

                <div class="flashcard" onclick="this.classList.toggle('revealed')">
                    <div class="flashcard-question">Can you just enter on any up or down candle with this technique?</div>
                    <div class="flashcard-answer">"you're not just indiscriminately going out and finding up candles and down candles... you're not just simply going in based on the candle itself by itself it's not a be all end-all and a system in and of itself"</div>
                </div>

                <div class="flashcard" onclick="this.classList.toggle('revealed')">
                    <div class="flashcard-question">What must you align with on the daily chart?</div>
                    <div class="flashcard-answer">"these conditions are best suited when we align them with a daily pd array in other words if there's a bearish order block if there's a gap that it's traded into if it's filled in a void if it's traded above a recent high okay or it's retreat back into an old historical low support broken analysis resistance"</div>
                </div>

                <div class="flashcard" onclick="this.classList.toggle('revealed')">
                    <div class="flashcard-question">What should monthly/weekly show for bearish sell limit setups?</div>
                    <div class="flashcard-answer">"on monthly and weekly if you're expecting lower prices or bearish pd arrays that should draw price down to a discount what you're expecting to see on the daily is up movement to go to a short term premium"</div>
                </div>

                <div class="flashcard" onclick="this.classList.toggle('revealed')">
                    <div class="flashcard-question">What feedback do you get when using this technique correctly?</div>
                    <div class="flashcard-answer">"you get quick immediate feedback even on a daily basis that you're on the right side of the marketplace and you start seeing profitability almost immediately"</div>
                </div>

                <div class="flashcard" onclick="this.classList.toggle('revealed')">
                    <div class="flashcard-question">How many pips was the first Japanese Yen example from September?</div>
                    <div class="flashcard-answer">"from that point all the way up to the weekly pd array or bearish order block it's 1800 pips"</div>
                </div>

                <div class="flashcard" onclick="this.classList.toggle('revealed')">
                    <div class="flashcard-question">Do you need intraday trading to make significant pips?</div>
                    <div class="flashcard-answer">"do you still think you need intraday trading to make pips hopefully after this teaching you'll quickly come to the conclusion that you do not need that"</div>
                </div>
            </div>
        </section>
    </main>

    <script>
        // Smooth scrolling for navigation
        document.querySelectorAll('nav a').forEach(anchor => {
            anchor.addEventListener('click', function (e) {
                e.preventDefault();
                const target = document.querySelector(this.getAttribute('href'));
                target.scrollIntoView({ behavior: 'smooth', block: 'start' });
            });
        });
    </script>
</body>
</html>